Moonlight for MLP1
Copyright (C) 2026 the contributors of this repository

This repository builds and packages Moonlight Embedded for the Miniloong
Pocket 1. It is a packaging and cross-compilation project; the streaming
client itself is upstream work, vendored verbatim under thirdparty/.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored sources
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

thirdparty/moonlight-embedded
    Moonlight Embedded, https://github.com/moonlight-stream/moonlight-embedded
    GNU General Public License v3.0 or later. Full text in LICENSE.
    Pinned commit: see scripts/upstream.lock.json.
    Modified in place by patches/0001-*.patch (see patches/README.md).

    Its own bundled third-party trees, carried here unchanged, are licensed as
    follows; the licence file shipped with each is kept alongside it:

    third_party/moonlight-common-c    LGPL-2.1+  (LICENSE.txt)
        enet/  (nested)               MIT        (enet/LICENSE)
    third_party/h264bitstream         LGPL-2.1+  (LICENSE)
    third_party/SDL_GameControllerDB  zlib       (LICENSE)
    third_party/ilclient              no licence file upstream
    third_party/libcec                no licence file upstream

    ilclient and libcec are not built: ENABLE_CEC is off and there is no
    Broadcom VideoCore on the RK3566.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Statically linked libraries
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The binary is a derived work of the libraries below. They are not vendored in
this repository; they are downloaded and cross-compiled into the toolchain
sysroot at build time by scripts/build-deps.sh, with versions pinned in
scripts/upstream.lock.json. Corresponds to the offer in GPL-3.0 section 13.

    ffmpeg 6.1.2      LGPL-2.1+ / GPL-2.0+ (configured --enable-gpl=no,
                      h264/hevc decoders only, no avformat/swscale)
    opus 1.5.2        BSD-3-Clause
    expat 2.x         MIT
    curl 8.x          curl (MIT-like)
    eudev 3.2.14      GPL-2.0+
    libevdev 1.13.3   MIT-like
    util-linux        BSD / GPL-2.0+ (libuuid only)
    OpenSSL 3.x       Apache-2.0
    libatomic         GPL-3.0+ with the GCC runtime library exception

    These come from the MLP1 toolchain sysroot and stay dynamically linked,
    so they are the device's concern, not this build's: glibc 2.38,
    SDL2 2.28.5 (zlib), ALSA (LGPL-2.1+), zlib (zlib).

